  "desc": "## Tavelo Arden\n\n**TAVELO ARDEN**\n\nNext-Generation All-Road Race Bike | Small\n\nThe Tavelo Arden is the next evolution of the brand that took the cycling world by storm. Debuted as a prototype at the 2026 Sea Otter Classic, Velo called it potentially the ultimate all-road race bike, a Tarmac with massive tyre clearance. This build pairs the Arden frameset with Shimano 105 Di2, the AVRO Rise cockpit, and Pertual Sharp carbon wheels.\n\nSPECIFICATIONS\n\n## Specifications\n\n- **Size:** Small\n- **Groupset:** Shimano 105 Di2, 12-Speed, wireless electronic shifting, hydraulic disc brakes\n- **Frame:** Tavelo Arden Carbon, claimed 650g in size M, wind-tunnel developed, BSA threaded BB, UDH, tyre clearance up to 38mm\n- **Fork:** Tavelo Arden Carbon, claimed 340g, aero-optimised\n- **Cockpit:** AVRO Rise Integrated Handlebar, internal cable routing\n- **Wheels:** Pertual Sharp Carbon, choice of 47/58 or 36/41 depth\n- **Tyres:** Continental Grand Prix, benchmark road rubber\n- **Certification:** UCI approved, EN ISO 4210 certified\n- **Condition:** Fully inspected and ready to ride\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\nFrameset also available separately for $2,380.\n\n## MKP Recommends\n\nThe Arden is one of the most talked-about frames in cycling right now, offering wind-tunnel-proven aero performance and a sub-700g frame at a fraction of what the big Western brands charge. Its standout over pure race bikes like the Tarmac is the 38mm tyre clearance and higher stack, so you get race speed with the versatility to run wider rubber for rough roads and light gravel. It is the rare bike that genuinely does everything.",
